## 4. Target Users, Personas & User Stories

### 4.1. Core Personas

| Persona | Title | Company Size | Key Pain Point | Typical Software Stack | Motivation to Pay |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Paul, the Owner/PM** | President / Senior PM | 5-25 employees (Small GC) | Lost a $50k profit on a job due to a 6-week unplanned historic review delay. Personally handles permits. | BuilderTrend, Excel, Dropbox. | Predictability. Needs a system so he can delegate permit tracking and take a vacation. |
| **Maria, the Compliance Manager** | Compliance & Safety Director | 50-200 employees (Mid-size GC) | Manages 30+ active projects. Nightmare is a sub's expired electric permit causing a site-wide Stop Work Order. | Procore, MS Project, Smartsheet. | Control & Audit Trail. Needs a single dashboard to prove compliance to insurers and owners. |
| **Ray, the Permit Expeditor** | Independent Consultant | 1-2 employees | Clients send incomplete plans, expecting magic. Spends hours on municipal websites. Billing is messy. | Email, QuickBooks, PDF Viewer. | Speed & Professionalism. A tool that gives him a competitive edge and justifies his fees. |

### 4.2. Detailed User Stories (By Role & Feature)

**For Paul, the GC Owner (Value: Speed to Bid)**
- **US-01:** As Paul, I upload an RFP's preliminary site plan so I can generate a permit requirements list and estimated fee schedule for my bid in under 30 minutes, not 2 days.
- **US-02:** As Paul, I want to re-use a "Scoop Template" from a previous similar project so I don't have to re-answer the same occupancy and building type questions.
- **US-03:** As Paul, I want to receive a weekly digest email summarizing the compliance status of all my active projects so I can spot problems without logging in.

**For Maria, the Compliance Manager (Value: Risk Mitigation)**
- **US-04:** As Maria, I want to see a real-time "Project Health Score" (0-100) for each job, calculated by the number of permits obtained vs. required, so I can prioritize my morning calls.
- **US-05:** As Maria, I want to receive an immediate push notification when the City of Austin updates a building code that impacts a structural permit on an active project so we can file a revision before the inspector arrives.
- **US-06:** As Maria, I want to invite our electrical subcontractor to the platform and require them to digitally attest that they have pulled their trade permits, creating a time-stamped audit log.

**For Ray, the Permit Expeditor (Value: Throughput & Billing)**
- **US-07:** As Ray, I want a client-facing portal where my GC clients can upload plans directly into my workflow, so I stop chasing missing files via email.
- **US-08:** As Ray, I want the platform to auto-populate standard municipal application forms with data extracted from the project profile, so I can cut 45 minutes of data entry per permit.
- **US-09:** As Ray, I want to track my time spent on each permit submittal and generate a professional, detailed invoice directly from the platform.

