## 7. System Architecture & Technical Specifications

### 7.1. High-Level Architecture
*(Conceptual Diagram in Text)*

**Client Layer**
[React Web App] [iOS/Android (V2)]
        ↓ (REST/GraphQL API via AWS API Gateway)

**API & Orchestration Layer (AWS ECS/Kubernetes)**
[Auth Service] → [Project Service] → [Intake Orchestrator]
                                     ↓
**AI Processing Pipeline (Event-Driven via AWS Step Functions/SQS)**
1. [Document Ingestion & Virus Scan]
2. [Computer Vision Microservice: Classify, OCR, Symbol Detect]
3. [NLP Microservice: NER & Scope Tagging]
4. [Rules Engine Microservice: Match Scope vs. Regulatory Graph]
5. [Report Aggregator: Build Permit List & Confidence Scores]
                                     ↓
**Data & State Layer**
[PostgreSQL (Tenant-Isolated)] → [AWS S3 (Plans)] → [Neo4j (Regulatory Graph DB)]
                                     ↓
**Monitoring & Notification Services**
[Elasticsearch] → [Code Change Crawler Engine] → [Alert Manager (WebSockets/Email)]

### 7.2. Technology Stack & Vendors
- **Frontend:** Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS UI.
- **Backend:** Node.js (core services), Python (AI microservices). GraphQL for main data API, REST for file uploads.
- **AI/ML:** AWS SageMaker for custom model training & hosting. AWS Textract for raw OCR. PyTorch for CV & NLP models. LangChain (controlled usage) for the "Chat with Your Plans" RAG feature (V2).
- **Database:** Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL (Transactional Data), Amazon Neptune (Managed Neo4j) for the Regulatory Graph.
- **File Storage:** AWS S3 with lifecycle policies to move "closed" project files to Glacier.
- **Search & Alerts:** Elasticsearch on AWS for full-text search of plan notes and code. WebSockets for real-time dashboard updates.
- **Auth:** Auth0 by Okta for RBAC and SSO integrations.
- **Monitoring:** Datadog for application performance, PagerDuty for on-call alerting.

### 7.3. Regulatory Graph Database Detailed Schema (Simplified)
- **Nodes:** `(:Jurisdiction {name: "City of Austin", type: "Municipal"})`, `(:CodeSection {id: "IBC_2021_907.2", text: "Where required..."})`, `(:Permit {name: "Commercial Building Permit", issuing_authority: "Austin Development Services"})`, `(:ScopeTag {name: "Fire Alarm", entity_type: "MEP"})`.
- **Relationships:** `(:ScopeTag)-[:TRIGGERS]->(:Permit)-[:GOVERNED_BY]->(:CodeSection)-[:ADOPTED_BY]->(:Jurisdiction)`. All relationships have `effective_date` and `superseded_by` properties for versioning.

