## 8. Data Model & Privacy

### 8.1. Core Data Objects
- **Organization:** Company name, billing plan, seats, address, default jurisdiction.
- **User:** Name, email, role (Owner, Manager, Expeditor), assigned Organization.
- **Project:** Address, valuation, occupancy type, construction type, work class, current stage, Compliance Health Score.
- **PlanSet:** A collection of uploaded `Document` objects, each with extracted metadata (OCR text, scope tags, class).
- **PermitRequirement:** A specific permit linked to a Project, with status (Required, Obtained, N/A), issuing authority, fees, timeline, and citations. This is the central unit of work.
- **AuditEvent:** Immutable log of: user action, timestamp, project ID, and details (e.g., "User:paul@xyz.com marked Permit E-01 as Obtained").

### 8.2. Data Privacy Policy
- **Data Ownership:** Users retain 100% ownership of all uploaded plans, project data, and generated reports. PermitAI claims no intellectual property over user data.
- **Data Processing Consent:** Users consent to their data being processed by cloud-hosted AI models. A specific opt-in is required for using their anonymized, aggregated data for AI model improvement.
- **Data Deletion:** Upon subscription cancellation, project data is preserved in a read-only state for 90 days (recovery window). After 90 days, all S3 files and database records are permanently purged via an automated, audited script. One-time exports (CSV/PDF) are offered during the 90-day window.

